        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108879845?u=eeb9306682180ab80521c80fd8f46609fe3c6770&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The output of the <code class=\"notranslate\">update-browser-releases</code> script is:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">@mdn/browser-compat-data@7.3.8 update-browser-releases<br>\nnode scripts/update-browser-releases/index.js --all</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Chrome for Desktop</strong>: Ignoring current version 147, which is not yet released (stable date is 2026-04-07).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Chrome for Android</strong>: Ignoring current version 147, which is not yet released (stable date is 2026-04-07).</p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Webview for Android</strong>: Ignoring current version 147, which is not yet released (stable date is 2026-04-07).</p>\n</div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Updates for Firefox for Desktop</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>New status for firefox 149: current, previously beta.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox 150: beta, previously nightly.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox 151: nightly, previously planned.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox 148: retired, previously current.</li>\n<li>New release detected for firefox: Version 152 as a planned release.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Updates for Firefox for Android</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>New status for firefox_android 149: current, previously beta.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox_android 150: beta, previously nightly.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox_android 151: nightly, previously planned.</li>\n<li>New status for firefox_android 148: retired, previously current.</li>\n<li>New release detected for firefox_android: Version 152 as a planned release.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"markdown-alert markdown-alert-note\" dir=\"auto\"><p class=\"markdown-alert-title\" dir=\"auto\"><svg class=\"octicon octicon-info mr-2\" viewBox=\"0 0 16 16\" version=\"1.1\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0 8a8 8 0 1 1 16 0A8 8 0 0 1 0 8Zm8-6.5a6.5 6.5 0 1 0 0 13 6.5 6.5 0 0 0 0-13ZM6.5 7.75A.75.75 0 0 1 7.25 7h1a.75.75 0 0 1 .75.75v2.75h.25a.75.75 0 0 1 0 1.5h-2a.75.75 0 0 1 0-1.5h.25v-2h-.25a.75.75 0 0 1-.75-.75ZM8 6a1 1 0 1 1 0-2 1 1 0 0 1 0 2Z\"></path></svg>Note</p><p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Opera for Desktop</strong>: No release announcement found among 10 items in <a href=\"https://blogs.opera.com/desktop/category/stable-2/feed/\" rel=\"nofollow\">this RSS feed</a>.</p>\n</div>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Updates for Safari for Desktop</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>New status for safari 26.3: retired, previously current.</li>\n<li>New status for safari 26.4: current, previously beta.</li>\n<li>New release date for safari 26.4: 2026-03-24, previously undefined.</li>\n<li>New engine version for safari 26.4: 624.1.16, previously 624.11.11.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Updates for Safari for iOS</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>New status for safari_ios 26.3: retired, previously current.</li>\n<li>New status for safari_ios 26.4: current, previously beta.</li>\n<li>New release date for safari_ios 26.4: 2026-03-24, previously undefined.</li>\n<li>New engine version for safari_ios 26.4: 624.1.16, previously 624.11.11.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Updates for WKWebView for iOS</h3>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>New status for webview_ios 26.3: retired, previously current.</li>\n<li>New status for webview_ios 26.4: current, previously beta.</li>\n<li>New release date for webview_ios 26.4: 2026-03-24, previously undefined.</li>\n<li>New engine version for webview_ios 26.4: 624.1.16, previously 624.11.11.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29334",
            "title": "Update browser releases",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-26T05:14:40.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-25T05:58:24.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "mdn-bot",
                "url": "https://github.com/mdn-bot"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/64103?u=428d3c27c9cd7efc648e17dfe5a4321c3f8e44d2&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Chrome has a couple of nasty bugs, which this PR captures as notes, with one triggering a partial implementation.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://crbug.com/364634040\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 364634040</a> reports that <code class=\"notranslate\">Clear-Site-Data</code> doesn't really take effect until a hard refresh or in a new tab. I took the version numbers in the report as true, since it was confirmed in the issue. I marked it as partial since the behavior is not feature detectable and the mitigation isn't really something developers can work around with a high expectation of success (e.g., asking users to do hard refreshes).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://crbug.com/40233601\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 40233601</a> reports long hangs on using the <code class=\"notranslate\">Clear-Site-Data</code> header. Large sites (GitHub and MDN) reported serious issues with this header; GitHub stopped using the header as a consequence. This one could be a partial, but I didn't set it because MDN kept using the header and the header <em>works</em> (in this case), just very slowly.</p>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://crbug.com/364634040\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 364634040</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://crbug.com/40233601\" rel=\"nofollow\">Bug 40233601</a></li>\n<li><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #12788.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"1022724032\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/12788\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/12788/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/12788\">#12788</a></li>\n</ul>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29333",
            "title": "`Clear-Site-Data`: record Chromium bugs",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T15:30:36.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-24T17:28:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ddbeck",
                "url": "https://github.com/ddbeck"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47647?u=2fbfc431a85d357f00c0146d5e55b425b7f00a3d&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Between versions 142 and 145, Chrome enables support for various features of the <a href=\"https://wicg.github.io/local-network-access/\" rel=\"nofollow\">Local Network Access spec</a>. See <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5152728072060928</a> and <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5068298146414592</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Specifically, these are:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">targetAddressSpace</code> <code class=\"notranslate\">Request</code> property, which was previously available behind a flag, and the equivalent <code class=\"notranslate\">RequestInit</code> property. AIUI, the property was finally enabled by default by version <code class=\"notranslate\">142</code>.</li>\n<li>The <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network-access</code> permission/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directive, which was added in 142.</li>\n<li>The more granular <code class=\"notranslate\">local-network</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">loopback-network</code> permissions/<code class=\"notranslate\">Permissions-Policy</code> directives, which were added in 145.</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR adds/updates data points as appropriate for these features.</p>\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29331",
            "title": "Chrome 142-145 support for local network access features",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T15:31:29.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-24T15:57:02.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "chrisdavidmills",
                "url": "https://github.com/chrisdavidmills"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105274?u=173310b843e2751843265438af8cfb79eda02039&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Apparently, <code class=\"notranslate\">font-stretch</code> is not only a CSS property and CSS descriptor, but it’s also an SVG attribute.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Since we have <a href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28809\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28809/hovercard\">undeprecated the property and descriptor</a>, the same applies to the attribute: the <code class=\"notranslate\">font-width</code> SVG attribute is currently supported only by Safari 18.4 and it’s impractical for developers to start using it yet.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3808464998\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28809\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28809/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28809\">#28809</a></li>\n<li><a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4128484826\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43567\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43567/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43567\">mdn/content#43567</a></li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29330",
            "title": "Undeprecate font-stretch SVG attribute",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-24T16:07:12.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-24T14:56:35.000Z",
