        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF140 adds support for  <code class=\"notranslate\">islamic-umalqura</code> calendar in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2011505\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2011505</a>. That means the option will appear in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Intl/supportedValuesOf\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Intl.supportedValuesOf</code></a> for the calendar option (<code class=\"notranslate\">console.log(Intl.supportedValuesOf(\"calendar\"));</code>) and can be used in the <code class=\"notranslate\">DataTimeFormat</code> constructor like this:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"const date = new Date();\n\nconst umAlQuraFormatter = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-u-ca-islamic-umalqura', {\n  calendar: 'islamic-umalqura',\n  dateStyle: 'full'\n});\n\nconsole.log(umAlQuraFormatter.format(date));\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">date</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Date</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-k\">const</span> <span class=\"pl-s1\">umAlQuraFormatter</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">new</span> <span class=\"pl-v\">Intl</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-c1\">DateTimeFormat</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s\">'en-u-ca-islamic-umalqura'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span> <span class=\"pl-kos\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">calendar</span>: <span class=\"pl-s\">'islamic-umalqura'</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"pl-c1\">dateStyle</span>: <span class=\"pl-s\">'full'</span>\n<span class=\"pl-kos\">}</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"pl-smi\">console</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">log</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">umAlQuraFormatter</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">.</span><span class=\"pl-en\">format</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">(</span><span class=\"pl-s1\">date</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">)</span><span class=\"pl-kos\">;</span></pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR is created to <strong>test</strong> whether BCD team wants to track support for languages and the other options - if you don't we can close this.<br>\nIt updates the <code class=\"notranslate\">DataTimeFormat</code> constructor to indicate the value is supported. Note that I didn't update <code class=\"notranslate\">supportedValuesOf()</code> because it is not a compatibility break to not support the value there.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I tested on chrome and Safari for the other versions in browserstack.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3977954198\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43203\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43203/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43203\">mdn/content#43203</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29323",
            "title": "FF149 Intl.DateTimeFormat supports islamic-umalqura calendar",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-23T23:53:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-23T23:50:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24025?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Deno supports <code class=\"notranslate\">Error.captureStackTrace</code> since v1.22.2.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">See: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4115842329\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\">#29313</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29313.\">Fixes</span>: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4115842329\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29313\">#29313</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29314",
            "title": "Update version_added for deno in `Error.captureStackTrace`",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-22T14:05:45.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-22T12:11:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "quad",
                "url": "https://github.com/quad"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7689582?u=11ee71fc041d4f515bef665b10af491bd2d2d5ab&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">With WebGPU support enabled by default in Safari 26 (shipped with macOS 26 Tahoe and iOS 26) a bunch of WebGPU features were enabled. All the features marked in this PR with <code class=\"notranslate\">\"version_added\" : \"26\"</code> were already available in previous Safari versions with the WebGPU flag enabled, and are now enabled by default.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Both <code class=\"notranslate\">core-features-and-limits</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">texture-formats-tier1</code> are enabled at least in Safari 26.2. I don't have access to a machine with 26.1 or 26.0 and I haven't found when they were added.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29309",
            "title": "Update WebGPU features for Safari",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-21T16:42:15.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-21T16:41:32.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "ferminLR",
                "url": "https://github.com/ferminLR"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@container\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">@container</code></a> selections where the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/At-rules/@container#container-query\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;container-query&gt;</code></a> part is optiona in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016474\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2016474</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This allows you to just select a container based on its name:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-css notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"@container --name {}\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-k\">@container</span> --name {}</pre></div>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This adds the subfeature. You can test this using <a href=\"https://wpt.live/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.live/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Note that I have set Chrome and Safari as <code class=\"notranslate\">false</code> but you can tell it is coming because they pass the test on the latest versions but NOT on current versions I can access: <a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-conditional/container-queries/query-container-name.html?label=master&amp;label=experimental&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Webkit: in STP release 235 <a href=\"https://webkit.org/blog/17739/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-235/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/blog/17739/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-235/</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3978053780\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43212\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43212/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43212\">mdn/content#43212</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29300",
            "title": "FF149 @container query is optional",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T16:21:26.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-20T01:24:22.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/495429?u=9d0bf7e5c07194485c7f81827005599ecced9712&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Marks Firefox as supporting CSS <code class=\"notranslate\">overflow-clip-margin</code> from 102.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The partial implementation referred to visual boxes already captured in subfeatures.</p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><span class=\"issue-keyword tooltipped tooltipped-se\" aria-label=\"This pull request closes issue #29268.\">Fixes</span> <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4082183767\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29268\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29268/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29268\">#29268</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29269",
            "title": "Firefox 102 added CSS `overflow-clip-margin`",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-20T21:19:35.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-16T13:07:55.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "caugner",
                "url": "https://github.com/caugner"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF149 adds support for CSS <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/font-family#math\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">font-family: math</code></a> property and applies it by default to the <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/MathML/Reference/Element/math\" rel=\"nofollow\"><code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;math&gt;</code></a> SVG element in <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014703\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2014703</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This follows on from <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4069112122\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/29250\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29250/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29250\">#29250</a> which added the note about the font-family. It adds info about versions that use the font family for math element.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3977999905\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43209\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43209/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43209\">mdn/content#43209</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29264",
            "title": "Chrome/Firefox/Safari apply `font-family: math` to `<math>` element",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T18:30:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-16T05:50:52.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">FF144 made a bunch of changes to support <code class=\"notranslate\">ShadowRoot.referenceTarget</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLTemplateElement.shadowRootReferenceTarget</code> and the corresponding attribute on the <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;template&gt;</code> element, and a new option to set this in <a href=\"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/attachShadow#referencetarget\" rel=\"nofollow\">`Element.attachShadow()</a> in  <a href=\"https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1981341\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1981341</a>.<br>\nThe spec changed slightly, and in FF149 it made the new additions nullable (which has no effect on a preferenced-only BCD feature).</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The PR <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3691450051\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/28570\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28570/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28570\">#28570</a> added some of these, but incorrectly indicated FF149 for FF support. It also missed the <code class=\"notranslate\">attachShadow()</code> option and <code class=\"notranslate\">HTMLTemplateElement.shadowRootReferenceTarget</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Explainer for the thing here <a href=\"https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md\">https://github.com/WICG/webcomponents/blob/gh-pages/proposals/reference-target-explainer.md</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">For FF I have updated to match the FF IDL. For Safari and Chrome I have copied the pattern of the features that were recorded - so exactly the same preferences and versions. I am making the assumption that these are implemented, because why wouldn't you.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">FYI <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/meyerweb/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/meyerweb\">@meyerweb</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4080141592\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43453\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/issues/43453/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43453\">mdn/content#43453</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29261",
            "title": "FF144 referenceTarget updates",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-16T04:34:28.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-16T04:22:41.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "hamishwillee",
                "url": "https://github.com/hamishwillee"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10931297?u=600cfcb4c4e709dfbc66b328147d846ee87b1e51&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Summary</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">We're adding <code class=\"notranslate\">loading=lazy</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;audio&gt;</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;video&gt;</code> attributes!</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Coming to Chrome in 147 (behind a flag): <a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">FYI: <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/scottjehl/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/scottjehl\">@scottjehl</a>  <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/hjanuschka/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/hjanuschka\">@hjanuschka</a></p>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Test results and supporting details</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">Audio:<br>\n<a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-audio-element?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Video:<br>\n<a href=\"https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://wpt.fyi/results/html/semantics/embedded-content/the-video-element?label=experimental&amp;label=master&amp;aligned</a></p>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://chromestatus.com/feature/5200068565139456</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Implementation bugs:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Chrome: <a href=\"https://crbug.com/469111735\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://crbug.com/469111735</a> -</li>\n<li>Firefox: <a href=\"https://bugzil.la/2005072\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://bugzil.la/2005072</a> (being implemented at: <a href=\"https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D278547\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D278547</a>)</li>\n<li>Safari: <a href=\"https://webkit.org/b/303995\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://webkit.org/b/303995</a> (being implemented at: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3917729684\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/issues/58220\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/WebKit/WebKit/pull/58220/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/WebKit/WebKit/pull/58220\">WebKit/WebKit#58220</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Firefox and Safari implementations are being actively worked on but, as per policy, I've left this marked as \"experimental\" until two implementations land in stable.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">More details:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><a href=\"https://scottjehl.com/posts/lazy-media/\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://scottjehl.com/posts/lazy-media/</a> (with a demo of it working)</li>\n<li><a href=\"https://www.januschka.com/chromium-video-lazy-loading.html\" rel=\"nofollow\">https://www.januschka.com/chromium-video-lazy-loading.html</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h4 dir=\"auto\">Related issues</h4>\n\n<p dir=\"auto\">See spec updates here: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3687064326\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11980\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/whatwg/html/pull/11980/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11980\">whatwg/html#11980</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Content PR: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"4072910479\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/43434\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/content/pull/43434/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43434\">mdn/content#43434</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Makes progress on: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"3968847431\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/809\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/mdn/mdn/issues/809/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/mdn/mdn/issues/809\">mdn/mdn#809</a></p>\n",
            "url": "https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/29256",
            "title": "Add `loading` attribute to audio and video",
            "date_modified": "2026-03-25T08:44:49.000Z",
            "date_published": "2026-03-13T15:34:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "tunetheweb",
                "url": "https://github.com/tunetheweb"
            }
        }
    ]
}